SUMMARY:Layer the Walls: Turn of the Century
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an educational and inspiring puppet play that explo
 res the stories of immigrant families in New York City—plus\, free kids'
  activities and crafts! In one Lower East Side tenement\, forty layers of 
 wallpaper were found clinging to the walls—each piece applied by a new i
 mmigrant family. Using puppetry\, masks\, and live action\, Layer the Wall
 s tells the incredible stories held within each layer—an Irish immigrant
  helping to build the Brooklyn Bridge\, Italian brothers surviving the Gre
 at Blizzard of 1888\, and two Russian Jewish garment workers joining the U
 prising of 20\,000 to fight for safety. Recommended for ages 8 and up. 2 p
 m • Free kids’ activities and crafts in the lobby!\n\nPrice: Not suppl
